   "discipline": "typescript",
   "risk": "low",
   "spec": "SCOPE NOTE: this item was re-verified live and is now narrowed to ONLY its sub-claim (1) \u2014 the help table renders `batch action` (a mandatory mount-namespace command) and `backlog create` (a host-namespace command whose leading `backlog` token is SILENTLY OPTIONAL) in visually identical shape. Sub-claims (2) (batch's calling convention) and (3) (opaque `{ input: object }` rendering) are ALREADY FIXED and require no further work \u2014 do not touch them.\n\nROOT CAUSE (verified by reading both files \u2014 the earlier grooming note's guess that this belongs in apigen-plugin-cli-output alone was only half right): `apigen-plugin-cli-output`'s `run()`/`formatUsage()` (packages/apigen/apigen-plugin-cli-output/src/lib/run.ts) has NO concept of an 'optional prefix' at all \u2014 it renders the literal, full `cli.path` key for every command verbatim, and rightly so: `resolveCommandPrefix`/`prefixCommand` (the functions that make `backlog` optional) are entrypoint/backlog/src/cli.ts-ONLY functions (verified: `rg -n \"prefixCommand|resolveCommandPrefix\" --type ts` outside entrypoint/backlog returns nothing) \u2014 this optionality is a host-specific UX convenience `backlog`'s own cli.ts bolts on BEFORE handing argv to apigen-plugin-cli-output's `run()`; the shared package genuinely cannot know 'backlog' is special unless told. So the fix threads an explicit, OPTIONAL annotation from the host through to the shared renderer \u2014 apigen-plugin-cli-output stays correct-by-default (empty annotation = current behavior, unchanged) for every OTHER apigen-hosted CLI that doesn't opt in.\n\nExact edits:\n1. File packages/apigen/apigen-plugin-cli-output/src/lib/run.ts. Change `function formatUsage(routes: Map<string, CliRoute>): string` (currently ~line 264) to accept a second parameter: `function formatUsage(routes: Map<string, CliRoute>, elidablePrefix: readonly string[] = []): string`. Inside its loop (currently iterating `sorted` and pushing `` `  ${key}${text ? ...}` ``), compute a display key that brackets the elidable leading segments when they match:\n```ts\nfor (const [key, { plan }] of sorted) {\n  const text = paramsText(plan.params);\n  const segs = key.split(' ');\n  const isElidable =\n    elidablePrefix.length > 0 &&\n    elidablePrefix.every((seg, i) => segs[i] === seg);\n  const displayKey = isElidable\n    ? `[${elidablePrefix.join(' ')}] ${segs.slice(elidablePrefix.length).join(' ')}`\n    : key;\n  lines.push(`  ${displayKey}${text ? `  { ${text} }` : ''}`);\n}\n```\n2. In `run()` (currently line 530 onward), read the new option once near where other `options[...]` reads already happen (mirror the existing loose-read style, e.g. near the `usePlugins`/`argv` reads): `const elidablePrefix = Array.isArray(input.options['cliElidablePrefix']) ? input.options['cliElidablePrefix'] as string[] : [];` and pass it as the 2nd argument at BOTH existing `formatUsage(routes)` call sites (the bare `--help`/empty-argv branch at ~line 680, and the 'Unknown command' `not_found` branch at ~line 693) \u2014 change both to `formatUsage(routes, elidablePrefix)`. Do NOT change the per-command detail-help branch (~line 702-704, `commandLabel` \u2014 a single already-disambiguated command, no ambiguity to resolve there).\n3. File entrypoint/backlog/src/cli.ts. At the `cliPlugin.run(...)` call site (currently ~line 602-620, inside the `options: {...}` object literal alongside `argv: prefixCommand(...)` and `usePlugins: [...USE_PLUGINS]`), add `cliElidablePrefix: prefix,` \u2014 reusing the ALREADY-COMPUTED `const prefix = resolveCommandPrefix(operations);` a few lines above in the same function (never a second, independently-derived list \u2014 mirrors this file's own existing `USE_PLUGINS`/`resolveMountNamespaces` never-drift convention documented in its own comments).\n\nAdd one test to the existing `describe('run() \u2014 help / usage listing (derived from the live command table)', ...)` block in packages/apigen/apigen-plugin-cli-output/src/test/run.spec.ts (reuse the file's existing `logSpy`/`makeInput` fixtures \u2014 read the file's top-of-file `beforeEach` for how `logSpy` is wired):\n```ts\nit('a declared cliElidablePrefix brackets the elidable segment in the summary table', async () => {\n  await run(\n    makeInput({\n      options: { argv: ['--help'], cliElidablePrefix: ['backlog'] },\n    })\n  );\n  const printed = logSpy.mock.calls[0][0] as string;\n  expect(printed).toContain('[backlog] get-item');\n  expect(printed).not.toContain('  backlog get-item');\n});\n```\n(The already-existing test 'empty argv prints the command listing... toContain(\"backlog get-item\")' immediately above, run WITHOUT `cliElidablePrefix`, is the negative-control regression guard proving default/unset behavior is unchanged \u2014 do not modify that test.)",
