   "spec": "File: packages/apigen/apigen-plugin-batch/src/lib/plugin.ts. `parseBatchRequest` (currently lines ~79-140) validates that `input['items']` is an Array (line ~106-111) but never inspects individual elements. `buildBatchHandler`'s returned handler (currently line ~155-210) then maps `request.items` into `RuntimeCall[]` with `domainArgs: (item ?? {}) as Record<string, unknown>` (currently line ~197), silently turning a null/undefined batch item into a no-arg call instead of rejecting the request.\n\nExact edits:\n1. In `parseBatchRequest`, immediately after the existing `if (!Array.isArray(items)) { throw ... }` check (currently ~line 106-111), add a per-element null/undefined check:\n```ts\nfor (let i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {\n  if (items[i] === null || items[i] === undefined) {\n    throw new ApiError(\n      'invalid_argument',\n      `@adhd/apigen-plugin-batch: \"input.items[${i}]\" must not be null or undefined`\n    );\n  }\n}\n```\nPlace this loop right after the existing `items` array-type check and before the `concurrency` field validation that follows it, so an invalid item is rejected before any other optional-field parsing runs (does not change behavior for any other field, only adds this new gate).\n2. In `buildBatchHandler`'s handler, change the `RuntimeCall[]` map's `domainArgs: (item ?? {}) as Record<string, unknown>` (currently line ~197) to `domainArgs: item as Record<string, unknown>` \u2014 the `?? {}` fallback becomes dead code once `parseBatchRequest` guarantees every element is non-null, so remove it rather than leave unreachable fallback logic (per the item's own explicit AC: 'No `?? {}` coercion remains on the item path').\n\nAdd one test to the existing `describe('batchPlugin handler: request validation', ...)` block in packages/apigen/apigen-plugin-batch/src/test/plugin.spec.ts (read the existing `it('rejects a non-array \"items\"', ...)` test at ~line 197 immediately above for the exact `mountedOp()`/`fakeCall()` fixture shape to reuse verbatim), named per the item's own Test Expectation:\n```ts\nit('batch with a null item is rejected with the item index', async () => {\n  const { op } = mountedOp();\n  await expect(\n    op.handler(fakeCall({ operation: 'ns/opA', items: [{ value: 'a' }, null] }))\n  ).rejects.toMatchObject({ code: 'invalid_argument', message: expect.stringContaining('items[1]') });\n});\n```",
